==Battleground==
*1 [[UltraBaaBaa]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Gardeneel Bros.]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Mega Baa Baa]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**Infinite [[Diabrollow]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.67 seconds<sup>2f~20f</sup>.

==Strategy==
As with Cubist Crimes, this gimmick stage forces the player to instantly destroy the frail base in one hit, or they'll be overwhelmed with a massive swarm of Diabrollows that destroy everything they touch. Fortunately, most of the other threats have long spawn delays, enabling the use of rusher units to quickly defeat them before moving onto the base. The use of a [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breaker]] is obviously necessary to get rid of the nasty UltraBaaBaa, and Gardeneel Bros. may Warp units ahead, causing them to inadvertently hit the enemy base and resulting in a loss.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Awakened Bahamut works just as well as he did in Cubist Crimes, with his high speed and extreme damage helping him to quickly reach and destroy the base. Meatshielding may be required to fend off Mega Baa Baa and Dogenstein, however.
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] - A slow, short-ranged rusher with extreme damage, 100% chance to destroy [[Barrier]]s and negligible health, Supercar makes for a good answer to UltraBaaBaa and can quickly remove her, though as it does not inflict enough damage to instantly destroy the base, it's better to deploy the unit a bit later.
**This changes if you have [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Diabolosa]], since [[Land-Air Assault (Combo)|Land-Air Assault]] paired with an Atk Sm [[Cat Combo|Combo]] allows Supercar to 1-shot the base. In this case, Supercar can be spawned immediately.

==Trivia==
*Wicked Clergyman may be a reference to "[[wikipedia:The Evil Clergyman|The Evil Clergyman]]", a short story by [[wikipedia:H. P. Lovecraft|H. P. Lovecraft]].

